-- src:797 | ⟦ח:קטע3|פרק ד סימן א|סימן א׳: פרשנות⟧
-- src:799 | סעיף 65 – פרשנות [תיקון: תשנ״ז, תשס״ט־4]
-- src:800 | (א) בפרק זה –

§§ `65(a) "insured"`

-- src:801 | ”מבוטח“ –
-- src:802 | (1) מבוטח לפי פרק י״א, למעט עקרת בית כהגדרתה בסעיף 238;
@ref National Insurance Law s 65(a) "מבוטח" (1) (source line 802)
GIVEN `the person` IS A `A person`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 65 "insured" (1) — insured under Chapter 11, other than a housewife` `the person` MEANS
        `the person`'s `insured under Chapter 11`
    AND NOT `the person`'s `a housewife as defined in section 238`

-- src:803 | (2) יחיד היושב בישראל, ואינו נעדר ממנה אלא העדר ארעי שהוא סביר, לדעת עובד המוסד שהוסמך לכך, ואין בו לסתור טענת אותו יחיד כי הוא יושב בישראל, ואינו מבוטח לפי פרק י״א, למעט עקרת בית כהגדרתה בסעיף 238;
@ref National Insurance Law s 65(a) "מבוטח" (2) (source line 803); the exception of a housewife is fork F18 (ruled by Meng, 2026-10-08, SHRUG)
GIVEN `the reading` IS A `A reading of a resident housewife under section 65 "insured" (2)`, `the person` IS A `A person`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 65 "insured" (2) — a resident of Israel not insured under Chapter 11, reading a resident housewife as` `the reading` `:` `the person` MEANS
        `the person`'s `resident in Israel`
    AND NOT `the person`'s `absent from Israel beyond a reasonable temporary absence`
    AND NOT `the person`'s `insured under Chapter 11`
    AND `limb (2)'s exception of a housewife, reading a resident housewife as` `the reading` `:` `the person`

-- Fork F18 (06-HW), RULED by Meng on 2026-10-08 (SHRUG): one named switch, declined by default.
-- Limb (2) ends "ואינו מבוטח לפי פרק י״א, למעט עקרת בית כהגדרתה בסעיף 238". Read as "and is not
-- insured under Chapter 11; excluding a housewife", a resident housewife is in neither limb: reading
-- (A), this row's in versions 0.1.0 to 0.2.0. Read as "and is not [insured under Chapter 11, other
-- than a housewife]", the noun phrase of limb (1) negated, she is insured under limb (2): reading
-- (B), the independent tester's (INDEPENDENT-FINDINGS.md, finding 4). The text does not decide, so
-- by default a case that turns on it is declined. The exception is reached only for a person who is
-- resident, not absent beyond a reasonable temporary absence, and not insured under Chapter 11 (the
-- conjunction above stops at the first that fails), so for anyone else the three readings agree.
@ref National Insurance Law s 65(a) "מבוטח" (2) (source line 803); fork F18; Meng's ruling of 2026-10-08 (SHRUG)
GIVETH A `A reading of a resident housewife under section 65 "insured" (2)`
`section 65 — the reading this row takes of a resident housewife under "insured" (2)` MEANS
    `a case that turns on a resident housewife's insurance is declined`

@ref National Insurance Law s 65(a) "מבוטח" (2) (source line 803): "למעט עקרת בית כהגדרתה בסעיף 238"; fork F18
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`section 65, in limb (2) of the definition of an insured person, does not say whether a resident housewife as defined in section 238, not insured under Chapter 11, is insured under it` MEANS
    REFUSE "section 65, in limb (2) of the definition of an insured person, does not say whether a resident housewife as defined in section 238, not insured under Chapter 11, is insured under it"

@ref National Insurance Law s 65(a) "מבוטח" (2) (source line 803): "למעט עקרת בית כהגדרתה בסעיף 238"; fork F18
GIVEN `the reading` IS A `A reading of a resident housewife under section 65 "insured" (2)`, `the person` IS A `A person`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`limb (2)'s exception of a housewife, reading a resident housewife as` `the reading` `:` `the person` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the reading`
    WHEN `a resident housewife is excluded from both limbs`
    THEN NOT `the person`'s `a housewife as defined in section 238`
    WHEN `a resident housewife is insured under limb (2)`
    THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a case that turns on a resident housewife's insurance is declined`
    THEN IF   `the person`'s `a housewife as defined in section 238`
         THEN `section 65, in limb (2) of the definition of an insured person, does not say whether a resident housewife as defined in section 238, not insured under Chapter 11, is insured under it`
         ELSE TRUE

@ref National Insurance Law s 65(a) "מבוטח" (source lines 801-803)
GIVEN `the reading` IS A `A reading of a resident housewife under section 65 "insured" (2)`
      `the person`  IS A `A person`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 65 — insured, reading a resident housewife as` `the reading` `:` `the person` MEANS
        "(1)" ... `s 65 "insured" (1) — insured under Chapter 11, other than a housewife` `the person`
    OR  "(2)" ... `s 65 "insured" (2) — a resident of Israel not insured under Chapter 11, reading a resident housewife as` `the reading` `:` `the person`

-- The rule of versions 0.1.0 to 0.2.0, by its old name, now at the reading the switch names.
@ref National Insurance Law s 65(a) "מבוטח" (source lines 801-803); fork F18
GIVEN `the person` IS A `A person`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 65 — insured` `the person` MEANS
    `s 65 — insured, reading a resident housewife as` `section 65 — the reading this row takes of a resident housewife under "insured" (2)` `:` `the person`

-- "one who was insured" (s 65 "ילד" (1)): a person who was insured and, on the day, is not.
@ref National Insurance Law s 65(a) "ילד" (1) (source line 805)
GIVEN `the reading` IS A `A reading of a resident housewife under section 65 "insured" (2)`
      `the person`  IS A `A person`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 65 — one who was insured, reading a resident housewife as` `the reading` `:` `the person` MEANS
        `the person`'s `formerly insured`
    AND NOT `s 65 — insured, reading a resident housewife as` `the reading` `:` `the person`

@ref National Insurance Law s 65(a) "ילד" (1) (source line 805); fork F18
GIVEN `the person` IS A `A person`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 65 — one who was insured` `the person` MEANS
    `s 65 — one who was insured, reading a resident housewife as` `section 65 — the reading this row takes of a resident housewife under "insured" (2)` `:` `the person`

§§ `65(a) "child" — whose child`

-- A child's record names its parents; the persons are found by name in the family. After
-- the family's facts are checked (nii-il06-family-on-a-day.l4) every name resolves to
-- exactly one person; before that, an unresolved name simply finds nobody.
GIVEN `the name`   IS A STRING
      `the family` IS A `A family on a day`
GIVETH A LIST OF `A person`
`the persons named` `the name` `in` `the family` MEANS
    filter (GIVEN p YIELD p's `name` EQUALS `the name`) (`the family`'s `the persons`)

-- (1) "the child of an insured or of one who was insured", read with s 1, under which
-- "child" includes a stepchild and an adopted child (fork F1): a natural, adoptive or step
-- relation makes the child the person's child.
-- src:170 | ”ילד“ – לרבות ילד חורג וילד מאומץ ולמעט נער ונערה נשואים;
@ref National Insurance Law s 65(a) "ילד" (1) (source line 805), s 1 "ילד" (source line 170)
GIVEN `the entry` IS A `A parent in a child's record`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the child is the person's child` `the entry` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the entry`'s `standing`
    WHEN `the child's natural parent`               THEN TRUE
    WHEN `the child's adoptive parent`              THEN TRUE
    WHEN `the child's step-parent`                  THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a person who is not the child's parent`   THEN FALSE

-- Version 0.3.0: the rules from here to the end of the section read "insured", so each takes the
-- reading of fork F18 that its caller passes on.
-- (2) "one who is not his child, if it is proven, to the satisfaction of whoever the
-- Administration authorised, that in the period set in regulations the insured supported him".
@ref National Insurance Law s 65(a) "ילד" (2) (source line 806)
GIVEN `the entry`   IS A `A parent in a child's record`
      `the family`  IS A `A family on a day`
      `the reading` IS A `A reading of a resident housewife under section 65 "insured" (2)`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 65 "child" (2) — the insured person named in` `the entry` `supported the child, in` `the family` `, reading a resident housewife as` `the reading` MEANS
        NOT `the child is the person's child` `the entry`
    AND `the entry`'s `support proven`
    AND any (GIVEN p YIELD `s 65 — insured, reading a resident housewife as` `the reading` `:` p) (`the persons named` (`the entry`'s `name of the person`) `in` `the family`)

@ref National Insurance Law s 65(a) "ילד" (1) (source line 805)
GIVEN `the entry`   IS A `A parent in a child's record`
      `the family`  IS A `A family on a day`
      `the reading` IS A `A reading of a resident housewife under section 65 "insured" (2)`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 65 "child" (1) — the child of an insured person, or of one who was insured, named in` `the entry` `, in` `the family` `, reading a resident housewife as` `the reading` MEANS
        `the child is the person's child` `the entry`
    AND any (GIVEN p YIELD `s 65 — insured, reading a resident housewife as` `the reading` `:` p OR `s 65 — one who was insured, reading a resident housewife as` `the reading` `:` p)
            (`the persons named` (`the entry`'s `name of the person`) `in` `the family`)

-- "the terms 'father', 'mother' and 'parent' shall be construed accordingly": the parents of
-- a child for this Chapter are the persons who make it a child under (1) or (2).
@ref National Insurance Law s 65(a) "ילד" (source lines 804-807)
GIVEN `the entry`   IS A `A parent in a child's record`
      `the family`  IS A `A family on a day`
      `the reading` IS A `A reading of a resident housewife under section 65 "insured" (2)`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 65 — a parent for this Chapter, named in` `the entry` `, in` `the family` `, reading a resident housewife as` `the reading` MEANS
        "(1)" ... `the child is the person's child` `the entry`
    OR  "(2)" ... `s 65 "child" (2) — the insured person named in` `the entry` `supported the child, in` `the family` `, reading a resident housewife as` `the reading`

-- The parents of the child for this Chapter who are insured on the day: the candidates s 67
-- chooses among. (A person who is "a parent" only under (2) is insured by definition.)
@ref National Insurance Law s 65(a) "מבוטח", "ילד" (source lines 801-807)
GIVEN `the child`   IS A `A child`
      `the family`  IS A `A family on a day`
      `the reading` IS A `A reading of a resident housewife under section 65 "insured" (2)`
GIVETH A LIST OF `A parent in a child's record`
`the insured parents of` `the child` `in` `the family` `, reading a resident housewife as` `the reading` MEANS
    filter (GIVEN e YIELD     `s 65 — a parent for this Chapter, named in` e `, in` `the family` `, reading a resident housewife as` `the reading`
                          AND any (GIVEN p YIELD `s 65 — insured, reading a resident housewife as` `the reading` `:` p) (`the persons named` (e's `name of the person`) `in` `the family`))
           (`the child`'s `parents`)

@ref National Insurance Law s 65(a) "ילד" (1) (source line 805)
GIVEN `the child`   IS A `A child`
      `the family`  IS A `A family on a day`
      `the reading` IS A `A reading of a resident housewife under section 65 "insured" (2)`
GIVETH A LIST OF `A parent in a child's record`
`the parents of` `the child` `who were insured, in` `the family` `, reading a resident housewife as` `the reading` MEANS
    filter (GIVEN e YIELD     `the child is the person's child` e
                          AND any (GIVEN p YIELD `s 65 — one who was insured, reading a resident housewife as` `the reading` `:` p) (`the persons named` (e's `name of the person`) `in` `the family`))
           (`the child`'s `parents`)

§§ `Days the later month lacks (fork F2; ruled by Meng, 2026-10-08, SHRUG)`

-- Two periods in this section end on a day reckoned from another: the 18th anniversary of a birth
-- (the proviso, "has reached 18") and three months from the day a child left Israel (s 65(b)).
-- Where that day does not exist in the later month (29 February in a common year; the 31st in a
-- month of 30 days; the 29th to the 31st in February), the Law does not say which day it is. Fork
-- F2, RULED by Meng on 2026-10-08 (SHRUG): one named switch, declined by default. Readings, kept
-- by name: the last day of the shorter month (`add years`, `add months`; this row's reading in
-- versions 0.1.0 to 0.2.0, and rows IL-05's and IL-08's); the 1st of the next month; or declined.
-- Declined means: a question whose answer turns on which of the two days it is is refused; one
-- whose answer is the same on both days is answered.
@ref National Insurance Law s 65(a) "ילד", proviso (source line 807), s 65(b) (source line 809); fork F2; Meng's ruling of 2026-10-08 (SHRUG)
GIVETH A `A reading of a day the later month lacks`
`section 65 — the reading this row takes of a day the later month lacks` MEANS
    `a case that turns on a missing day is declined`

@ref National Insurance Law s 65(a) "ילד", proviso (source line 807), s 65(b) (source line 809); fork F2
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`the Law does not say on which day a period ends that would end on a day the later month lacks, such as 29 February in a common year` MEANS
    REFUSE "the Law does not say on which day a period ends that would end on a day the later month lacks, such as 29 February in a common year"

-- Where two readings give one answer, that answer; otherwise the refusal.
@ref fork F2
GIVEN `on the last day of the shorter month` IS A BOOLEAN
      `on the 1st of the next month`         IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the same answer on both days, or declined:` `on the last day of the shorter month` `and` `on the 1st of the next month` MEANS
    IF   `on the last day of the shorter month` EQUALS `on the 1st of the next month`
    THEN `on the last day of the shorter month`
    ELSE `the Law does not say on which day a period ends that would end on a day the later month lacks, such as 29 February in a common year`

-- A day moved on by a number of months (`add months` clamps; the anniversary uses `add years`,
-- which is `add months` by twelve times as many), read as the reading says.
@ref fork F2
GIVEN `the day`         IS A DATE
      `the clamped day` IS A DATE
      `the reading`     IS A `A reading of a day the later month lacks`
GIVETH A DATE
`the day` `moved on, clamped to` `the clamped day` `, reading a missing day as` `the reading` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the reading`
    WHEN `a missing day clamps to the last day of the shorter month` THEN `the clamped day`
    WHEN `a missing day rolls to the 1st of the next month`          THEN `rolled`
    WHEN `a case that turns on a missing day is declined`
    THEN IF   `rolled` EQUALS `the clamped day`
         THEN `the clamped day`
         ELSE `the Law does not say on which day a period ends that would end on a day the later month lacks, such as 29 February in a common year`
    WHERE
        `rolled` MEANS
            IF   DATE_DAY `the clamped day` LESS THAN DATE_DAY `the day`
            THEN `add months` (YMD (DATE_YEAR `the clamped day`) (DATE_MONTH `the clamped day`) 1) 1
            ELSE `the clamped day`

§§ `65(a) "child" — the proviso: in Israel, and under 18`

-- "has not reached 18 years": the day is before the 18th anniversary of the birth. For a
-- birth on 29 February the anniversary in a common year is a day the month lacks: fork F2, above.
-- src:807 | ובלבד שהילד נמצא בישראל ולא מלאו לו 18 שנים; והמונחים ”אב“, ”אם“ ו”הורה“ יתפרשו בהתאם לכך.
@ref National Insurance Law s 65(a) "ילד", proviso (source line 807); fork F2
GIVEN `the child`   IS A `A child`
      `the reading` IS A `A reading of a day the later month lacks`
GIVETH A DATE
`the 18th anniversary of the birth of` `the child` `, reading a missing day as` `the reading` MEANS
    (`the child`'s `date of birth`) `moved on, clamped to` (`add years` (`the child`'s `date of birth`) 18) `, reading a missing day as` `the reading`

-- By its old name, at the reading the switch names: declined for a birth on 29 February, whose
-- 18th anniversary always falls in a common year.
@ref National Insurance Law s 65(a) "ילד", proviso (source line 807); fork F2
GIVEN `the child` IS A `A child`
GIVETH A DATE
`the 18th anniversary of the birth of` `the child` MEANS
    `the 18th anniversary of the birth of` `the child` `, reading a missing day as` `section 65 — the reading this row takes of a day the later month lacks`

@ref National Insurance Law s 65(a) "ילד", proviso (source line 807); fork F2
GIVEN `the day`     IS A DATE
      `the child`   IS A `A child`
      `the reading` IS A `A reading of a day the later month lacks`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 65 — under 18 on` `the day` `:` `the child` `, reading a missing day as` `the reading` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the reading`
    WHEN `a case that turns on a missing day is declined`
    THEN `the same answer on both days, or declined:` (`read as` `a missing day clamps to the last day of the shorter month`) `and` (`read as` `a missing day rolls to the 1st of the next month`)
    OTHERWISE `read as` `the reading`
    WHERE
        `read as` r MEANS `the day` LESS THAN `the 18th anniversary of the birth of` `the child` `, reading a missing day as` r

@ref National Insurance Law s 65(a) "ילד", proviso (source line 807); fork F2
GIVEN `the day`   IS A DATE
      `the child` IS A `A child`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 65 — under 18 on` `the day` `:` `the child` MEANS
    `s 65 — under 18 on` `the day` `:` `the child` `, reading a missing day as` `section 65 — the reading this row takes of a day the later month lacks`

§§ `65(b) — a child out of Israel`

-- src:809 | (ב) לא יראו ילד כנמצא בחוץ לארץ אם יצא מישראל לתקופה שאינה עולה על שלושה חודשים; אולם המוסד רשאי לראותו כאילו הוא בישראל גם אם יצא מישראל לתקופה העולה על שלושה חודשים.
-- "left Israel for a period not exceeding three months": the period runs from the day the
-- child left to the day the child returned, or, for an absence not yet ended, to the day
-- asked about (fork F3). Three months from a day the later month lacks: fork F2, above.
-- "Not exceeding" is inclusive.
@ref National Insurance Law s 65(b) (source line 809); fork F2
GIVEN `the day`     IS A DATE
      `the absence` IS AN `An absence from Israel`
      `the reading` IS A `A reading of a day the later month lacks`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 65(b) — the absence, as at` `the day` `, is for a period not exceeding three months:` `the absence` `, reading a missing day as` `the reading` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the reading`
    WHEN `a case that turns on a missing day is declined`
    THEN `the same answer on both days, or declined:` (`read as` `a missing day clamps to the last day of the shorter month`) `and` (`read as` `a missing day rolls to the 1st of the next month`)
    OTHERWISE `read as` `the reading`
    WHERE
        `the day of leaving` MEANS `the absence`'s `the day the child left Israel`
        `read as` r MEANS `the end of the period` AT MOST (`the day of leaving` `moved on, clamped to` (`add months` `the day of leaving` 3) `, reading a missing day as` r)
        `the end of the period` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the absence`'s `the day the child returned to Israel`
            WHEN JUST `the day of return` THEN `the day of return`
            WHEN NOTHING                  THEN `the day`

@ref National Insurance Law s 65(b) (source line 809); fork F2
GIVEN `the day`     IS A DATE
      `the absence` IS AN `An absence from Israel`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 65(b) — the absence, as at` `the day` `, is for a period not exceeding three months:` `the absence` MEANS
    `s 65(b) — the absence, as at` `the day` `, is for a period not exceeding three months:` `the absence` `, reading a missing day as` `section 65 — the reading this row takes of a day the later month lacks`

-- "A child shall not be regarded as abroad if he left Israel for a period not exceeding three
-- months; but the Institute may regard him as if he is in Israel even if he left for a period
-- exceeding three months." Version 0.3.0 asks the Institute's decision first: where it regards the
-- child as in Israel, the length of the absence, and so fork F2, is not reached. The answer is the
-- same in every other case.
@ref National Insurance Law s 65(b) (source line 809); fork F2
GIVEN `the day`     IS A DATE
      `the child`   IS A `A child`
      `the reading` IS A `A reading of a day the later month lacks`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 65 — in Israel on` `the day` `:` `the child` `, reading a missing day as` `the reading` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the child`'s `absence from Israel`
    WHEN NOTHING          THEN TRUE
    WHEN JUST `the absence` THEN
            "אולם המוסד רשאי לראותו כאילו הוא בישראל" ... `the child`'s `the Institute regards the child as in Israel`
        OR  "(ב) לא יראו ילד כנמצא בחוץ לארץ" ... `s 65(b) — the absence, as at` `the day` `, is for a period not exceeding three months:` `the absence` `, reading a missing day as` `the reading`

@ref National Insurance Law s 65(b) (source line 809); fork F2
GIVEN `the day`   IS A DATE
      `the child` IS A `A child`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 65 — in Israel on` `the day` `:` `the child` MEANS
    `s 65 — in Israel on` `the day` `:` `the child` `, reading a missing day as` `section 65 — the reading this row takes of a day the later month lacks`

§§ `65(a) "child" — the definition`

-- s 1 excludes "a married boy or girl" from "child"; s 65 is read with it (fork F1).
@ref National Insurance Law s 1 "ילד" (source line 170)
GIVEN `the child` IS A `A child`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 1 — not a married boy or girl` `the child` MEANS
    NOT `the child`'s `married`

-- The two readings this row takes where the text does not decide (forks F18 and F2), as one
-- record that the rules of ss 65-68 pass on (version 0.3.0).
GIVEN `the reading of a resident housewife` IS A `A reading of a resident housewife under section 65 "insured" (2)`
      `the reading of a missing day`        IS A `A reading of a day the later month lacks`
GIVETH A `The readings this model takes where the text does not decide`
`reading a resident housewife as` `the reading of a resident housewife` `and a missing day as` `the reading of a missing day` MEANS
    `The readings this model takes where the text does not decide` WITH
        `for a resident housewife under section 65 "insured" (2)` IS `the reading of a resident housewife`
        `for a day the later month lacks`                         IS `the reading of a missing day`

@ref forks F18 and F2; Meng's ruling of 2026-10-08 (SHRUG)
GIVETH A `The readings this model takes where the text does not decide`
`the readings this row takes where the text does not decide` MEANS
    `reading a resident housewife as` `section 65 — the reading this row takes of a resident housewife under "insured" (2)`
        `and a missing day as` `section 65 — the reading this row takes of a day the later month lacks`

