§§ `65(a) "child", the proviso's age limb, for a month section 72 pays`

-- Version 0.2.0 (06-S72). s 72(a) pays the allowance from the 1st of the month in which
-- entitlement arose, if it arose by the 15th, and to the last day of the month in which it
-- ceased. So in the month of an 18th birthday the child is paid for although, from the birthday
-- on, it has "reached 18"; and in the month of a birth by the 15th it is paid for although,
-- before the birth, there is no child. s 72 is not encoded in this row (row IL-08 encodes it):
-- which children it pays for in a month is the caller's answer, the children of `A family in a
-- month`. This row reads s 72(a) only to say which of them s 65's age limb lets through for the
-- month: a child whose 18th birthday (fork F2 where it is a day the month lacks) is on or after
-- the month's first day, and who is born by its last. A listed child outside that is a problem
-- with the facts (nii-il06-family-on-a-day.l4), not a child left out.
-- src:854 | (א) נוצרה זכאות לקצבת ילדים עד 15 בחודש פלוני, תשולם הקצבה החל ב־1 באותו חודש; נוצרה הזכאות אחרי 15 בחודש פלוני, תשולם הקצבה החל ב־1 בחודש שלאחריו; תשלום הקצבה יסתיים ביום האחרון של החודש שבו נפסקה הזכאות.

@ref National Insurance Law s 72(a) (source line 854): "ב־1 באותו חודש"
GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the first day of the month of` `the day` MEANS
    YMD (DATE_YEAR `the day`) (DATE_MONTH `the day`) 1

@ref National Insurance Law s 72(a) (source line 854): "ביום האחרון של החודש"
GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day of the month of` `the day` MEANS
    YMD (DATE_YEAR `the day`) (DATE_MONTH `the day`) (`Days in month` `the day`)

@ref National Insurance Law s 65(a) "ילד", proviso (source line 807), read with s 72(a) (source line 854); fork F2
GIVEN `the day`     IS A DATE
      `the child`   IS A `A child`
      `the reading` IS A `A reading of a day the later month lacks`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 65, read with s 72(a) — not 18 before the month of` `the day` `began, and born by its end:` `the child` `, reading a missing day as` `the reading` MEANS
        "תשלום הקצבה יסתיים ביום האחרון של החודש שבו נפסקה הזכאות" ... `not 18 before the month began`
    AND "נוצרה זכאות לקצבת ילדים עד 15 בחודש פלוני" ...           `the child`'s `date of birth` AT MOST `the last day of the month of` `the day`
    WHERE
        `not 18 before the month began` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the reading`
            WHEN `a case that turns on a missing day is declined`
            THEN `the same answer on both days, or declined:` (`read as` `a missing day clamps to the last day of the shorter month`) `and` (`read as` `a missing day rolls to the 1st of the next month`)
            OTHERWISE `read as` `the reading`
        `read as` r MEANS `the 18th anniversary of the birth of` `the child` `, reading a missing day as` r AT LEAST `the first day of the month of` `the day`

@ref National Insurance Law s 65(a) "ילד", proviso (source line 807), read with s 72(a) (source line 854); fork F2
GIVEN `the day`   IS A DATE
      `the child` IS A `A child`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 65, read with s 72(a) — not 18 before the month of` `the day` `began, and born by its end:` `the child` MEANS
    `s 65, read with s 72(a) — not 18 before the month of` `the day` `began, and born by its end:` `the child` `, reading a missing day as` `section 65 — the reading this row takes of a day the later month lacks`

-- The age limb, for the question asked: under 18 on the day; or, for the month s 72 pays, not 18
-- before the month began and born by its end.
@ref National Insurance Law s 65(a) "ילד", proviso (source line 807); s 72(a) (source line 854)
GIVEN `the question` IS A `The question asked of a family on a day`
      `the reading`  IS A `A reading of a day the later month lacks`
      `the day`      IS A DATE
      `the child`    IS A `A child`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 65 — the age limb, asked` `the question` `, reading a missing day as` `the reading` `, on` `the day` `:` `the child` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the question`
    WHEN `the allowance on the family's day`
    THEN `s 65 — under 18 on` `the day` `:` `the child` `, reading a missing day as` `the reading`
    WHEN `the allowance for the month of the family's day, for the children section 72 pays for in it`
    THEN `s 65, read with s 72(a) — not 18 before the month of` `the day` `began, and born by its end:` `the child` `, reading a missing day as` `the reading`

§§ `A family in a month, as a family on its day`

-- `A family in a month` (nii-il06-nouns.l4) put as a family on the day its facts stand on, its
-- children being the ones s 72 pays for in the month. Every rule of ss 65-68 that takes a family on
-- a day answers the month when asked `the allowance for the month of the family's day, …`.
GIVEN `the family` IS A `A family in a month`
GIVETH A `A family on a day`
`the family in a month, on its day:` `the family` MEANS
    `A family on a day` WITH
        `the day`        IS `the family`'s `a day in the month, on which the facts stand`
        `the persons`    IS `the family`'s `the persons`
        `the children`   IS `the family`'s `the children section 72 pays for in the month`

@ref National Insurance Law s 65(a) "ילד" (source lines 804-807), s 1 "ילד" (source line 170), s 72(a) (source line 854)
GIVEN `the family` IS A `A family in a month`
      `the child`  IS A `A child`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 65 — a child for this Chapter, for the month section 72 pays, in` `the family` `:` `the child` MEANS
    `the answer to` (GIVEN r YIELD `s 65 — a child for this Chapter, asked` `the allowance for the month of the family's day, for the children section 72 pays for in it`
                                       `, reading` r `, in` `the day's family` `:` `the child`)
        `at` `the readings this row takes where the text does not decide`
        `, fork F18 mattering:` (`fork F18 can matter in` `the day's family`) `, fork F2 mattering:` (`fork F2 can matter for` `the child`)
        `, two answers merged by` (GIVEN x, y YIELD IF x EQUALS y THEN JUST x ELSE NOTHING)
    WHERE
        `the day's family` MEANS `the family in a month, on its day:` `the family`

§§ `A question at readings that include the declined one (version 0.3.0)`

-- How a question is answered where a reading the caller passes, by name or through a switch, is
-- the declined one. The question is answered at each of the two other readings of that fork; if
-- `the merge` finds the two answers the same, that is the answer, otherwise the question is
-- declined by the fork's refusal. F18 is taken first, then F2, so with both declined the question
-- is answered at up to four pairs of readings. Where a fork cannot matter to the question (no
-- resident housewife not insured under Chapter 11 among the persons; no birth on 29 February and
-- no absence that began on a 29th, 30th or 31st), the readings agree by construction and the
-- question is answered once, at the first reading. A question that one of the two readings itself
-- declines for another reason (s 69A, s 71, s 67(b)) is declined with that reason.
-- Meng's ruling of 2026-10-08 (SHRUG), as the lead set it on 2026-10-08: decline only where the
-- readings give different answers to the question asked.
@ref forks F18 and F2; Meng's ruling of 2026-10-08 (SHRUG)
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
      `the question`        IS A FUNCTION FROM `The readings this model takes where the text does not decide` TO a
      `the readings`        IS A `The readings this model takes where the text does not decide`
      `F18 matters`         IS A BOOLEAN
      `F2 matters`          IS A BOOLEAN
      `the merge`           IS A FUNCTION FROM a AND a TO MAYBE a
GIVETH AN a
`the answer to` `the question` `at` `the readings` `, fork F18 mattering:` `F18 matters` `, fork F2 mattering:` `F2 matters` `, two answers merged by` `the merge` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the housewife`
    WHEN `a case that turns on a resident housewife's insurance is declined`
    THEN IF   `F18 matters`
         THEN CONSIDER `the merge` (`at the housewife's reading` `a resident housewife is excluded from both limbs`) (`at the housewife's reading` `a resident housewife is insured under limb (2)`)
              WHEN JUST `the answer` THEN `the answer`
              WHEN NOTHING           THEN `section 65, in limb (2) of the definition of an insured person, does not say whether a resident housewife as defined in section 238, not insured under Chapter 11, is insured under it`
         ELSE `at the housewife's reading` `a resident housewife is excluded from both limbs`
    OTHERWISE
         CONSIDER `the missing day`
         WHEN `a case that turns on a missing day is declined`
         THEN IF   `F2 matters`
              THEN CONSIDER `the merge` (`the question` (`at the missing day's reading` `a missing day clamps to the last day of the shorter month`)) (`the question` (`at the missing day's reading` `a missing day rolls to the 1st of the next month`))
                   WHEN JUST `the answer` THEN `the answer`
                   WHEN NOTHING           THEN `the Law does not say on which day a period ends that would end on a day the later month lacks, such as 29 February in a common year`
              ELSE `the question` (`at the missing day's reading` `a missing day clamps to the last day of the shorter month`)
         OTHERWISE `the question` `the readings`
    WHERE
        `the housewife`   MEANS `the readings`'s `for a resident housewife under section 65 "insured" (2)`
        `the missing day` MEANS `the readings`'s `for a day the later month lacks`
        `at the housewife's reading` h MEANS
            `the answer to` `the question` `at` (`reading a resident housewife as` h `and a missing day as` `the missing day`)
                `, fork F18 mattering:` FALSE `, fork F2 mattering:` `F2 matters` `, two answers merged by` `the merge`
        `at the missing day's reading` d MEANS
            `reading a resident housewife as` `the housewife` `and a missing day as` d

-- Where fork F18 can matter: a person whom limb (2)'s exception of a housewife reaches.
@ref National Insurance Law s 65(a) "מבוטח" (2) (source line 803); fork F18
GIVEN `the person` IS A `A person`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`fork F18 can matter for` `the person` MEANS
        `the person`'s `resident in Israel`
    AND NOT `the person`'s `absent from Israel beyond a reasonable temporary absence`
    AND NOT `the person`'s `insured under Chapter 11`
    AND `the person`'s `a housewife as defined in section 238`

GIVEN `the family` IS A `A family on a day`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`fork F18 can matter in` `the family` MEANS
    any `fork F18 can matter for` (`the family`'s `the persons`)

-- Where fork F2 can matter: a birth on 29 February (`add years` clamps no other day), or an
-- absence that began on a 29th, 30th or 31st (`add months` by three clamps no other).
@ref National Insurance Law s 65(a) "ילד", proviso (source line 807), s 65(b) (source line 809); fork F2
GIVEN `the child` IS A `A child`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`fork F2 can matter for` `the child` MEANS
        (DATE_DAY (`the child`'s `date of birth`) EQUALS 29 AND DATE_MONTH (`the child`'s `date of birth`) EQUALS 2)
    OR  (CONSIDER `the child`'s `absence from Israel`
         WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
         WHEN JUST a  THEN DATE_DAY (a's `the day the child left Israel`) AT LEAST 29)

GIVEN `the family` IS A `A family on a day`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`fork F2 can matter in` `the family` MEANS
    any `fork F2 can matter for` (`the family`'s `the children`)
